  "body": "## What\n\nBoth shipped templates \u2014 and both root copies \u2014 carried a real `github.repo` and two real numeric user ids in `triggers.allowlist`. `config generate` writes the minimal template **verbatim** as the operator's `config.yaml`.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nAn operator who edits `repo` and forgets `allowlist` has allowlisted two foreign accounts on their own repository. Those accounts can then summon paid reviews and get the agent posting under the operator's token. `AGENTS.md` \u00a7RESTRICTIONS says real account identifiers never enter the repository; the templates were the one place they did.\n\n## How\n\n- Both templates now carry `repo: owner/name` and `allowlist: []` (all four files: root + packaged).\n- `_startup.load_config` refuses the literal `owner/name` (`PLACEHOLDER_REPO`), so `config validate`, `host check` and `daemon start` all stop on a generated-and-unedited file.\n- An empty allowlist stays **valid** \u2014 it is the documented safe starting state \u2014 but `load_config` logs a WARNING and `config validate` prints one to stderr, because \"the agent never answers\" and \"nobody is allowlisted\" look identical from the outside.\n- `docs/CONFIG.md` and `docs/TOKENS.md` no longer print the real ids.\n\n**Why the refusal is at the startup layer, not in `Config.load`:** the templates have to stay parseable, because `tests/test_config.py` loads them to prove the docs and the loader have not drifted. \"Well-formed\" and \"ready to run\" are different questions, and only the commands that are about to poll, spend or post need the second one.\n\nOne real id remains in `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-18-review-engine-seam-design.md`. That is a dated design record, not published by mkdocs and not shipped in the wheel; rewriting history seemed worse than leaving it. Say the word and I will scrub it too.\n\n## Tests\n\n- two parametrized tests that neither shipped example names a real account, and that each is parseable but **not** runnable (`StartupError`, matching `placeholder`);\n- `config generate` output does not `config validate` until `repo` is changed;\n- a generated config with a real repo validates `0` and warns about the empty allowlist;\n- the existing template tests now assert the placeholders.\n\n## Gate\n\n```\n1020 passed, 2 skipped, 1 deselected, 1 warning in 73.55s\nruff format / ruff check: clean\npylint src 9.95/10   pylint tests 9.36/10\npyright: 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 informations\n```\n\nReleases **1.1.2**. Based on `fix/61-usage-limit-markers` (#93) \u2014 GitHub will retarget this to `main` once that merges.\n\nFixes #62.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
